        {
          "id": "the_short_model_year_group_is_a_property_of_the_pollutant_process",
          "description": "The one cohort key that is a property of the pollutant-process rather than of the cohort, and the reason the rate stage rides a flat (pollutant-process x cohort) relation rather than widening the cohort's own columns (docs/esm-conventions.md 27.1). `pollutantprocessmodelyear` maps model year 1980 to modelYearGroup 1980 for the energy pollutant-processes, whose `shortModYrGroupID` is 80 -- a two-digit year -- and to modelYearGroup 19781995 for the refueling ones, whose short group is 52; at 1998 the two are 98 and 5300. Model year 2020 is 40 for both, which is why the pair has to be checked at more than one model year to be checked at all. A two-dimensional column keyed on both would not be a join key: `join.rs` resolves a key through a declared 1-D variable's single axis.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
